{
    desc => q{Two consecutive Ctrl-d scrolls two half-pages},
    description => <<'END_DESC',
## Macro: `xt/visual/macros/scrolling/ctrl_d_twice`

Tests that two consecutive `Ctrl-d` keystrokes scroll the viewport down by
approximately one full page (two half-pages). The buffer has 40 numbered
lines so the cumulative scroll is clearly visible.

Keys: `Ctrl-d` then `Ctrl-d`

- **ctrl_d_twice_initial.png**: Cursor at line 1 col 0 on "scroll line 1".
- **ctrl_d_twice_after_first.png**: After first `Ctrl-d`, viewport scrolled down ~half a page.
- **ctrl_d_twice_after_second.png**: After second `Ctrl-d`, viewport scrolled down ~one full page total.
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('Control-d');
        $ctx->delay(200);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_first');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('Control-d');
        $ctx->delay(200);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_second');
    },
}
